 **Subagents are read-only.** A Claude subagent's `herdr-threads`/`ht` calls carry `--agent-id=<id>`, inserted by the PreToolUse hook; Codex subagents are enrolled from their start events (Hermes delegate children register from their `subagent_start` events). The CLI refuses a subagent's write before it reaches the daemon (`unsupported`, exit 4), and the daemon refuses any subagent-role binding with `subagent_read_only` (exit 1) for every accountable command (check-in, handoff, create thread, invite, join, accept, reject, send, ACK, leave, topic and name changes, archive, reopen). Subagents read and summarize their own stream (`inbox`, whose display advances only their own binding's cursor and ACKs nothing, as does a full `body ID` read, `inbox --machine`, `read`, `summary`, ...) and advance only their own binding's cursor; the top-level agent does the ACKs. This is cooperative: the Claude rewrite recognizes simple commands that run `herdr-threads` or `ht`, and a shape it does not recognize (`eval`, `bash -c`, scripts, `$(...)`, a quoted or path-qualified command word) stays attributed to the parent session and is not refused.
 
