+Accepting the active invitation to a direct one-to-one thread preserves each binding's existing cursor and seeds missing open-binding cursors at the invitation's timeline event, keeping opening messages available. Acceptance is not display: each binding retains its own unread stream even when a sibling shows the message. A new binding while the invitation is pending can independently receive that episode's addressed lazy messages; a new binding after acceptance uses the normal joined-thread seeding rule (the seat's furthest cursor, or the head if none exists).
 
 **Human exclusivity.** A person's seat (`human me init`) holds only the person's binding and is refused (see `me init` refusals above) while an agent binding of the seat is connected, unless `--operator`. Any agent enrollment, reconnect or plain call on a human seat ends the human binding; a later resume enrolls a fresh binding.
 
 **Presence.** See the presence fields below: `active` means at least one open connected binding (or the person's open binding on a seat still resolved onto its pane); `inactive` means none. Availability, wake targeting and the archival rule all follow connected bindings.
 
 **Wake, pane close and archival.** A wake is decided per connected top-level binding placed on the observed terminal (subagent, disconnected, ended and human bindings are never targets); a pane's mod channel is per binding. A closed pane retires its seat: every connected binding disconnects with reason `seat_retired` and its cursors are kept. A thread archives after one quiet hour only when no member has a connected binding (a human member counts while its pane exists); bindings migrated from the single-occupant model count as active for 24 hours after the upgrade.
 
 **Upgrading.** Re-run `herdr-threads setup` (and `setup hermes --profile NAME`) so the SessionStart, SubagentStart/SubagentStop, Codex SessionEnd and Hermes finalize hooks are installed; `doctor` and `setup-status` report a `stale_install` finding naming the missing events and the exact `herdr-threads setup HARNESS` fix (`the installed claude integration lacks ...: re-run ... (agents started before the upgrade also need a restart)`). A binding migrated from the older model is re-adopted, cursors kept, by the first agent call whose session id matches the one it recorded; idle agents that have not made a call since the upgrade are not woken until they do.
 
